.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3385:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter1.log:55:In Stage 1 scenarios and checklists are **not separate lists** — each scenario carries an **attached checklist** of concrete yes/no conditions that, if all satisfied, prove the scenario is handled. Adversarial coverage (edge cases / failure modes / attack vectors) is baked into the scenarios at frame-build time, not deferred to a separate adversarial sub-stage. Stage 2 walks each perspective's locked Frame once.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3386:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter1.log:65:The job of evaluation: **find the problems the creator missed**. It is not a confirmation step. A `PASS` verdict without findings must be defensible — "looks fine" is not a finding.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3387:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter1.log:105:Review stance is "find ways this will fail". Not "is this good?" — that question collapses into agreement with the creator. A `PASS` verdict that did not actively try to break the artifact is unreliable. **Comfort is a warning sign.** If the agent feels comfortable with the artifact, it has not pushed hard enough.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3388:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter1.log:282:- `scenario_gap` and `checklist_gap` findings — **constructive**: on `PASS`, MEMORIZATION stages them under `staging/scenarios/` and `staging/checklists/` for Wrap-up to promote
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3389:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter1.log:323:| 3 | If `n ≥ 2`: each prior-iter finding inherited at Stage 1 | Judge its **current `disposition:`** based on the artifact: `addressed` (resolved by a change in this artifact iteration — cite the resolution evidence), `open` (still present, unchanged), `disputed` (creator pushed back with rationale; record both creator and evaluator positions), `deferred` (moved to backlog with pointer), `superseded` (replaced by a more general / specific finding — cite the new ID). Iter 1 skips this step | Per-finding disposition update |
