.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3496:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:151:| `sessions/{date}-{session-id}/{loop}/staging/decisions/{slug}.md` (with `mistake-candidate: true`) | assistant (MEMORIZATION) | PASS only — one file per mistake-candidate, stamped with `decisions.md` template |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3497:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:406:In Stage 1 scenarios and checklists are **not separate lists** — each scenario carries an **attached checklist** of concrete yes/no conditions that, if all satisfied, prove the scenario is handled. Adversarial coverage (edge cases / failure modes / attack vectors) is baked into the scenarios at frame-build time, not deferred to a separate adversarial sub-stage. Stage 2 walks each perspective's locked Frame once.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3498:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:416:The job of evaluation: **find the problems the creator missed**. It is not a confirmation step. A `PASS` verdict without findings must be defensible — "looks fine" is not a finding.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3499:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:456:Review stance is "find ways this will fail". Not "is this good?" — that question collapses into agreement with the creator. A `PASS` verdict that did not actively try to break the artifact is unreliable. **Comfort is a warning sign.** If the agent feels comfortable with the artifact, it has not pushed hard enough.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/wrap-up/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:3500:.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/rawdata/codex-eval-stdout-iter2.log:633:- `scenario_gap` and `checklist_gap` findings — **constructive**: on `PASS`, MEMORIZATION stages them under `staging/scenarios/` and `staging/checklists/` for Wrap-up to promote
