.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f/execution/task-07/staging/learnings/dual-system-cross-mirror-drift-detection.md:21:Cross-mirror drift (`CLAUDE.md` fixed but `AGENTS.md` not, or vice versa) is a recurring class of defect in this repo. Without a system that checks each mirror from its own perspective, the drift silently survives evaluation — the PASS is valid from one system's view but the defect persists in the other's entrypoint. Every cross-mirror change needs dual-system evaluation to be trustworthy.
